  "worked_solution": "We wish to compute the probability that a student plays violin *given that* they don't play guitar. Therefore, we need to compute $P(V|{G}^{′}).$  \n\nTo compute $P(V|{G}^{′}),$ we need to ask, \"what is the probability of $V$ occurring given that $G$ has *not* occurred?\"\n\nSince we are assuming that $G$ has *not* occurred, we only consider the students outside $G.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14273146/assets/fe7d08bfcd72d7851cecdc65abaa85f16a1249f51bc9b3ece843a93cad23b5cc.png)\n\nIn total, the number of students in the set ${G}^{′}$ is \n\n$$\n35+10=45.\n$$\n\nOf these $45$ students, $35$ lie inside $V.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14273146/assets/683e832c719ca5ba0a054fe8d29579c4dbb82097cf14c74d72f5843964922f94.png)\n\nSince each outcome is equally likely, $P(V|{G}^{′})$ can be interpreted as the proportion of $V$ that lies inside ${G}^{′},$ relative to the size of ${G}^{′}.$ Therefore, we have\n\n$$\nP(V|{G}^{′})=\\frac{35}{45}=\\frac{7}{9}.\n$$",
